          }
        },
        {
          "say": "So halving the volume shifts right, making more ammonia.",
          "write": "halve V → more NH₃"
        },
        {
          "say": "With equal gas moles on each side, like H two and I two, no shift.",
          "write": "equal moles: no shift"
        },
        {
          "say": "Adding argon at constant volume changes nothing. No shift.",
          "write": "inert gas: no shift"
        },
        {
          "say": "Diluting a solution shifts towards more dissolved particles.",
          "write": "dilute → more particles"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Changing temperature",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Temperature is the only change that alters K.",
          "write": "only T changes K"
        },
        {
          "say": "Treat heat as a product of an exothermic reaction.",
          "write": "exo: heat is a product"
        },
        {
          "say": "Heat it, and an exothermic equilibrium shifts left. K decreases.",
          "write": "heat exo → left, K ↓"
        },
        {
          "say": "Two NO two makes N two O four, exothermic. In ice, it goes paler.",
          "write": "2NO₂ ⇌ N₂O₄, ΔH < 0",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "Hot tube brown, cold tube pale",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
